{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474162-gangrel-and-ventrue-disciplines","id":1474162,"title":"Gangrel and Ventrue disciplines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-07T22:24:33-08:00","id":1474162,"title":"Gangrel and Ventrue disciplines","content":"It might have been discussed over the years, but why do the Gangrel and Ventrue share the same clan disciplines: Animalism and Resilience?<br /> <br /> I prefer to mix up the preconceptions from VtM so I have shifted the Ventrue clan disciplines to Animalism, <i>Dominate</i> and Vigor, while also shifting the Nosferatu clan disciplines to Obfuscate, <i>Nightmare</i> and Resilience. Gives a symmetry between the clan discipline spread, and provides for variation. Gives a better feel to the Nosferatu as unrelenting terror.<br /> <br /> What is your experience?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","user":"Cabaal","date":". 02-08-2022, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T23:27:27-08:00","id":1474166,"title":"","content":"Mostly because they [sort of] share the same root curse that they mutated/evolved/deviated from.<br /> <br /> The specific details are weird, and someone more rooted in Requiem's metaphysics and history will probably better explain it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T00:32:08-08:00","id":1474169,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, it could be a sort of a convergent evolution happening between two strains of predators who share the MO of \u2018stay in control of your surroundings.\u2019<br /> <br /> Maybe it\u2019s both \u2014 it seems that not all members of a given Clan necessarily descend from the same source\u2026<br /> <br /> Nosferatu with Resilience sound fun though. Nothing says Scary like someone walking towards you with knives sticking out of their eye sockets yet completely unfazed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T00:43:28-08:00","id":1474170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474162-gangrel-and-ventrue-disciplines?p=1474169#post1474169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, it could be a sort of a convergent evolution happening between two strains of predators who share the MO of \u2018stay in control of your surroundings.\u2019<br /> <br /> Maybe it\u2019s both \u2014 it seems that not all members of a given Clan necessarily descend from the same source\u2026<br /> <br /> Nosferatu with Resilience sound fun though. Nothing says Scary like someone walking towards you with knives sticking out of their eye sockets yet completely unfazed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll note my answer isn't provided as some kind of &quot;What if&quot; answer postulate. Requiem is not my strongest language in the overall Chronicles universe, but that answer is provided out of sense of hearing someone mentioning it in a book.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Nosferatu, the Haunt's freakish strength is better played for their entire aesthetic than some kind of resilience, the boogeyman emerged from shadow at your throat, your every effort falling short to break their rip on your body, your heart, your mind. Of the two, they are not the ones I'd change.<br /> <br /> As for the Ventrue, meh, if you wanna change them up, I'd offer the Julii route of Dominate, Vigor, and Resilience, but the unflappable lord of the castle is a strong and compelling image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T00:56:54-08:00","id":1474171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474162-gangrel-and-ventrue-disciplines?p=1474170#post1474170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll note my answer isn't provided as some kind of &amp;quot;What if&amp;quot; answer postulate. Requiem is not my strongest language in the overall Chronicles universe, but that answer is provided out of sense of hearing someone mentioning it in a book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, not sure what you meant by this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regarding the Nosferatu, the Haunt's freakish strength is better played for their entire aesthetic than some kind of resilience, the boogeyman emerged from shadow at your throat, your every effort falling short to break their rip on your body, your heart, your mind. Of the two, they are not the ones I'd change. </div> </div> </div>Heh, that reminds me of a horror story skit on YouTube (sorta like a Korean creepypasta channel) that featured a ghost-thing showing <i>exactly</i> that. I was indeed giddily whispering \u201cNosferatu!\u201d back then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T01:11:27-08:00","id":1474173,"title":"","content":"1e ran with the idea that Ventrue and Gangrel shared an origin. In 2e it's less clear because the commonly assumed previous form of the Ventrue (aka the Julii) have changed away from both Ventrue and Gangrel, meaning they're either convergent or that the Ventrue didn't come from the Julii (which was implied to the point where you couldn't reasonably argue otherwise in first edition) but rather split from Gangrel at some other time.<br /> <br /> As for the Disciplines, Animalism fits both Clans. The Ventrue because it's another venue of lording over other creatures, and the Gangrel as another connection to their animalistic themes.<br /> Resilience works great for Gangrel as the hardy, outdoorsy survivor type, but it's not something slots naturally into the Ventrue, imo. But none of the physical Disciplines really do. I'd say that Vigor fits a bit better, but not moreso than the other Clans' physical Disciplines. It wouldn't be surprised if the 1e devs decided on Ventrue's physical Discipline last and chose Resilience because it's the only one that otherwise wouldn't be shared with another Clan.<br /> <br /> Vigor works great for Nosferatu, though. It fits very naturally with Obfuscate, while Resilience with Obfuscate leads to defensive double dipping where you can neither see your target nor damage it once you do. Same with Celerity and Obfuscate with the &quot;I'm not here&quot; angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T08:50:26-08:00","id":1474202,"title":"","content":"Resilience fits Ventrue as another aspect of making them above and separate from their lessers. They are untouchable nobles; in this case, untouchable includes near-invulnerability.<br /> <br /> Ventrue are lords - untouchable and commanding of man and beast<br /> Gangrel are beasts - they share an affinity with the animals and survive where others could not","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T15:03:16-08:00","id":1474231,"title":"","content":"Coincidentally, I wrote about this the other day for [reasons]:<br /> <br /> So, the lore is intentionally contradictory about this subject. There are a few theories:<br /> <br /> 1) The Gangrel were the younger clan, and the Ventrue were Savages who &quot;learned&quot; Dominate and became something different: <i>\u201cMarauding Gangrel tore through Eastern Europe. Some of their number broke away from the packs to settle down and become masters of men. They abandoned the mutable flesh and discovered the Lordly Tongue. Some say these alphas evolved to a more sophisticated forest. Others say the Lords are a weak offshoot of the Savages, little brother choking on a razorwire noose of repression.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> 2) The Ventrue were the younger clan, and the Gangrel are Lord offshoots who went feral and learned to shapeshift. The Julii in this case are possibly the Ventrue in a different form or an unrelated clan with a similar power: <i>\u201cIn the wastes outside the Roman Empire, barbarians fornicated with savage gods. The bestial offspring of these couplings craved blood, and one fed upon Gnaeus of Ventrue. The Lord\u2019s blood debased the creature, and it became like him, a feral Kindred of a kind.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> 3) Clans Gangrel, Julii, and Ventrue are siblings, but the significance of this link is murky. It may be that all three are connected to the Strix more intimately than the other clans: The Julii because they made a deal to master the All Night Society, the Ventrue because they stole the Julii\u2019s niche (and possibly helped the Strix destroy them), and the Gangrel because their Discipline is maybe-kinda-sorta slowly turning them all into Strix.<br /> <br /> These are only three possible permutations! There are lots of ways to think of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-16T03:36:51-08:00","id":1497270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474162-gangrel-and-ventrue-disciplines?p=1474231#post1474231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the lore is intentionally contradictory about this subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I've always liked about Requiem vs Masquerade. In Requiem the past is blurry and no one knows the true origin of vampires or even if there is one or more such origins. Kinda why I miss the fog of eternity of 1st edition since it reinforced why vampires didn't knew their roots and gave total liberty to the GMs. Heck, under 1st edition, no vampire except for a very few exceptions remembers clearly any events that happened prior to the 16th century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3638,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3638-daganisoraan","user":"Daganisoraan","date":". 11-16-2022, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3638-daganisoraan","name":"Daganisoraan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-16T05:10:03-08:00","id":1497273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daganisoraan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1474162-gangrel-and-ventrue-disciplines?p=1497270#post1497270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I've always liked about Requiem vs Masquerade. In Requiem the past is blurry and no one knows the true origin of vampires or even if there is one or more such origins. Kinda why I miss the fog of eternity of 1st edition since it reinforced why vampires didn't knew their roots and gave total liberty to the GMs. Heck, under 1st edition, no vampire except for a very few exceptions remembers clearly any events that happened prior to the 16th century.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Truth be told, while i did make considerable use of some of the concepts connected to the Fog in my own chronicles to amp the mystery &amp; strangeness in relation to Masquerade, as others pointed out the unreliability of individual memory, ubiquitous presence of Dominate, miscommunication between supernatural beings and a number of other factors can explain the uncertainty of facts well enough without the Fog as a sort of barrier. Overall it's not gone per se so much as considerably downplayed.<br /> <br /> (Being honest here - i used and abused it <b>a lot</b> of the Fog, specially by picking some concepts about Torpor from Mythologies to outright twist and blend with astral journey mechanics, goetian demons &amp; more from MtAw and some pre-Geist Book of Dead stuff, a gate to my own personal <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1472918-vampire-otherworld?p=1473170#post1473170\">vampire otherworld</a>, basically)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-16-2022, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-16T11:15:18-08:00","id":1497298,"title":"","content":"Honestly, from an outside perspective you can piece together a very rough idea of how kindred came about (it's probably related to the Strix Synthesis power), and even in-universe there's actual knowledge going back to Ancient Rome (even if it's nowhere near comprehensive). But vampires don't know their origins, and any who were around for it are more alien than most Methuselahs.<br /> <br /> The sheer extent of the lack of knowledge as presented in the 1e core is at least partially an overreaction to Masquerade latching on to the whole Caine thing. But it's not a bad thing, and 2e reigned in the bits that weren't strictly needed to make it believable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}